From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raag Jadav <raag.jadav@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:42:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] drm/xe/pci_error: Flush GT wedge worker before bus reset

With GT wedging now done async, make sure the wedge worker is flushed to
avoid side-effects during PCI bus reset.

Fixes: 13b9555ffb03 ("drm/xe/xe_pci_error: Implement PCI error recovery callbacks")
Signed-off-by: Raag Jadav <raag.jadav@intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Rodrigo Vivi <rodrigo.vivi@intel.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261022051303.282805-7-raag.jadav@intel.com
Signed-off-by: Matt Roper <matthew.d.roper@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Akanksha Hotta <akanksha.hotta@intel.com>
(cherry-picked from commit 0dbc1d0762bc89649aeaea98a63f6e5f786ea1b8 linux-next)
Signed-off-by: Akanksha Hotta <akanksha.hotta@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pci_error.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pci_error.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pci_error.c
index 8c7e8f24c276..8e512bbf2034 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pci_error.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pci_error.c
@@ -31,8 +31,10 @@ static void prepare_device_for_reset(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 
 	xe_device_set_in_reset(xe);
 
-	for_each_gt(gt, xe, id)
+	for_each_gt(gt, xe, id) {
 		xe_gt_declare_wedged(gt);
+		flush_work(&gt->wedge.worker);
+	}
 
 	pci_disable_device(pdev);
 }
-- 
